# nlt-fusion — Cursor Rules

## Governance

- Read `NLT-DEV-OTOI.md` before making any changes. It is the canonical agent contract.
- Joshua W. Dorsey, Sr. is final authority on all architectural, deployment, UX, and strategic decisions. Escalate — do not guess.
- Follow commit format: `[AGENT_NAME] type(scope): description`
- No LLM provider lock-in, no architecture decisions, no production deployments, no credential storage, no external integrations without explicit Joshua approval.

## Codebase Layout

- `world-engine/` — All application code (React frontend + Python simulation engine)
- `world-engine/src/` — Python simulation engine (ECS world engine, avatars, aides, NPCs, scenarios)
- `world-engine/*.jsx`, `world-engine/index.html` — React frontend prototype (CDN-loaded, no build step)
- Root level — Governance infrastructure (AGENTS.md, NLT-DEV-OTOI.md, SOPs, templates)

## Python Engine

- Python source uses relative imports (`from ..core.events import ...`).
- Missing core modules: `src/avatars/base_avatar.py`, `src/aides/base_aide.py`, `src/fusion/readiness_assessor.py`, `src/database/supabase_client.py`. Do not stub these without Joshua's approval.
- No `__init__.py` files exist yet. Do not add without Joshua's approval on package structure.
- No `requirements.txt` or `pyproject.toml` exists. Dev tools (flake8, pytest) are installed via pip.

## Frontend Prototype

- No package.json, no bundler, no build step. React 18 + Babel loaded from CDN.
- Serve with any static file server: `cd world-engine && python3 -m http.server 8765`
- Do not introduce a build pipeline unless the prototype is promoted to `apps/`.

## Lint and Validation

- `flake8 world-engine/src/ --select=E9,F63,F7,F82` — must pass with 0 errors
- `python3 -m compileall world-engine/src/` — must compile cleanly
- `bash .nltotoi/scripts/validate-governance.sh` — must pass before any governance file changes
